      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nPrune `docs/`, `docker/`, `recipes/`, `.buildkite/`, `.github/`, and `.agents/` from the sdist. The sdist drops from 49.7 MB to 23.7 MB, and the wheel built from it is unchanged.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The sdist shrinks by about 52% (49.7 MB to 23.7 MB on current `main`). The v0.33.0 sdist on PyPI is 47.1 MB.\n- No build or test input is removed. `tests/`, `examples/`, `benchmarks/`, `tools/`, `rust/`, `csrc/`, `cmake/` and `requirements/` all stay.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll runs are on `main` @ ff74259da3, using the release recipe `python setup.py sdist` (`.buildkite/scripts/upload-release-wheels-pypi.sh`).\n\n| | sdist size | files |\n|---|---|---|\n| before | 49,732,506 B | 8,833 |\n| after | 23,746,768 B | 7,973 |\n\n- **What gets dropped:** diffing the two sdist file lists shows only the pruned directories go: docs (364 files), .buildkite (218), recipes (193), .github (44), .agents (23) and docker (18). Nothing is added.\n- **CUDA configure:** a CMake configure from the extracted pruned sdist succeeds (`TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=9.0`, CUDA 13.0, Ninja). That covers `tools/build_deepgemm_C.py`, the external projects, and so on.\n- **Wheel contents:** `VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=empty uv build --wheel --no-build-isolation` works from both sdists. The two wheels have identical file lists (3,833 files, excluding dist-info).\n- **Downstream packagers:** I checked conda-forge's [vllm-feedstock](https://github.com/conda-forge/vllm-feedstock). It builds from the PyPI sdist and runs `pytest ./tests/...` from it. Its patches only touch `CMakeLists.txt`, `cmake/`, `requirements/`, `tools/build_deepgemm_C.py` and `vllm/`, none of which are pruned.\n\nI did not run a full CUDA compile from the pruned sdist. The configure step plus the identical file lists cover the files the build reads.\n\n## Details\n\n`pyproject.toml` enables setuptools-scm, and setuptools-scm's file finder adds every git-tracked file to the sdist. `MANIFEST.in` only ever added files, so the sdist shipped the whole repo. Half of it was `docs/assets`: a 7.3 MB HTML timeline, two architecture PNGs of 4.9 MB and 4.0 MB, and many screenshots.\n\nThere is no PyPA rule here. The [sdist spec](https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/source-distribution-format/) requires only `pyproject.toml` and `PKG-INFO`. The [package formats guide](https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/discussions/package-formats/) says sdists \"commonly\" include tests and docs. In the [discuss.python.org thread](https://discuss.python.org/t/should-sdists-include-docs-and-tests/14578), distro and conda-forge packagers asked for tests so they can run the suite. So `tests/` stays, as conda-forge relies on it. Docs, CI config and Dockerfiles go: the docs build from git on ReadTheDocs, and nothing downstream builds or tests from those directories.\n\nDuplicate check: no open PR touches sdist contents. #54551 also edits `MANIFEST.in`, but it removes the `LICENSE` include, which is unrelated.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
